# Secrets and local tool state (docs/deploy.md). Never commit these.
.env*
!.env.example
.dev.vars*
.wrangler/
docker/secrets/
*.pem
# ONE named exception to `*.pem`: the CA intermediate that
# www.parkinginfo.ntpc.gov.tw does not send, without which New Taipei cannot
# build a chain and fails every tick (docs/sources.md, "Known limits"). It is a
# PUBLIC certificate and nothing else -- no private key is committed anywhere
# in this repo, and none should ever be. The file's own header block says what
# it is and where it came from.
#
# Keep this list at one entry. The rule above is a deliberate guard, and a hole
# carved in it for convenience is how such guards stop meaning anything; test
# fixtures in particular never need one (see tests/test_sources_tls.py, which
# proves certificate rejection with a public certificate and no key at all).
!src/parkcast/sources/twca-ssl-ca-2023.pem
worker/node_modules/
web/.dev-artifacts/
# Brainstorm mockups and SDD ledgers (superpowers plugin scratch)
.superpowers/
# Isolated worktrees for in-progress plans
.claude/worktrees/
.worktrees/

# Web app
web/node_modules/
web/dist/
# Dev copies of the collector output (see scripts/sync-artifacts.mjs)
web/public/artifacts/
# Basemap archive (~23 MB) and the tiles unpacked from it, both regenerable via
# scripts/build-basemap.mjs (see docs/basemap.md). The label glyphs in
# web/public/basemap/fonts/ are small and committed.
web/basemap-src/
web/public/basemap/tiles/
# Offline place index, regenerable via scripts/build-place-index.mjs
web/public/places/
